    <!-- The sound driver is a Z80 program kept compressed in the cartridge. The game's 68000 decompresses it into the
         Z80's RAM, copies a few constants after it, then for each song decompresses that song's data into the Z80's RAM
         (at 0x1000), writes the song's request number to the driver's request byte and releases the Z80 from reset (the
         driver clears its variables when it starts but keeps a request that is already there, so warmup_frames is 0).
         Requests: 0x81-0xAC songs (each with its own block of data), 0xB0-0xF2 sound effects (they work with
         any song loaded, so the first is used), other numbers do not make a sound. The driver has no request that
         silences everything: Music Stop starts the Machine again. -->
